Package: pdfsigner
Version: 0.7.0-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Homero Thompson del Lago del Terror <noreply@example.com>
Installed-Size: 386
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, libnss3-tools, python3-cryptography, python3-pil, python3-lxml, python3-yaml, python3-requests, python3-certifi, python3-tz
Recommends: opensc, pcscd, libengine-pkcs11-openssl
Suggests: yubikey-manager, libetoken11
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/vdirienzo/pdfsigner
Description: Sign PDF documents with USB cryptographic tokens
 PDFSigner is a GTK4/libadwaita application for digitally signing
 PDF documents using PKCS#11 USB cryptographic tokens.
 .
 Features:
  * PAdES-LTV signatures with TSA timestamps
  * Support for multiple token types (SafeNet, YubiKey, Nitrokey, OpenSC)
  * Batch signing with PIN cache
  * Visible signature stamps
  * Signature validation
  * CLI and GUI interfaces
 .
 Supported tokens include SafeNet eToken, YubiKey PIV, Nitrokey,
 and any OpenSC-compatible smart card.
